# Cloudinary Implementation Standards

This rule ensures all media assets are optimized, secure, and consistently handled across the SalesOps project.

## 1. Image Delivery & Optimization
Always prioritize performance and cost-efficiency by using automatic formatting and quality.

- **Mandatory Transformations**: Every image URL or component must include:
  - `f_auto`: Automatically deliver the best format (WebP/AVIF) based on the browser.
  - `q_auto`: Automatically adjust compression level to balance quality and file size.
- **Sizing**: Never serve raw, full-resolution images. Always specify width (`w_`) and height (`h_`) using `c_fill` or `c_limit`.

## 2. Component Usage (React/Next.js)
When using Cloudinary in the frontend:
- Use the `@cloudinary/react` library instead of plain `<img>` tags where possible.
- **Placeholder**: Always provide a `blur` or `pixelate` placeholder for a better LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) experience.

Example:
```tsx
import { AdvancedImage } from '@cloudinary/react';
import { fill } from "@cloudinary/url-gen/actions/resize";

// Standard implementation
const myImage = cld.image('sample_id').resize(fill().width(400).height(300));
<AdvancedImage cldImg={myImage} />